INT. MEAT-PACKING COLD STORAGE - NIGHT

Steel racks. Hanging sides of beef in plastic. Breath clouds. A single caged bulb.

ROCCO DELAVEGA, fifties, in a wool overcoat, stands with his back to a swinging carcass. IMANI BROOKSHIRE-ADE, thirties, in a puffy parka, holds a duffel bag. DUTCH PELLEGRINO, forties, scarf over his mouth, keeps one hand in his pocket.

ROCCO
Count it.

IMANI
I counted it.

ROCCO
Count it again.

She unzips the bag. Stacks of bills, rubber-banded. She thumbs one. Dutch watches her hands.

DUTCH
Light.

IMANI
It's not light.

DUTCH
It's light.

ROCCO
(quiet)
Is it?

Imani shoves the bag across the floor. Dutch pulls his hand from his pocket. A pistol. Imani's own gun clears the parka at the same instant. Rocco steps between them, palms up, and all three freeze.

ROCCO (CONT'D)
Put them down.

IMANI
You first.

DUTCH
You first.

IMANI
He's lying.

DUTCH ^
She's lying.

Rocco lowers his hands and, with a sigh, takes a step back into the swinging beef. He hits it with his shoulder. The carcass swings out, across the frame, between Imani and Dutch.

They lunge. The pistols go off together, twice. Meat jerks on its hook. Rocco drops flat. Imani rolls behind a rack. Dutch scrambles for the bag, clawing at the zipper.

DUTCH (CONT'D)
(muttering)
Come on, come on...

Silence. A drip from the ceiling. Three people breathing hard in the cold.

ROCCO
(from the floor)
Anyone hit?

IMANI
(from behind the rack)
No.

DUTCH
No.

ROCCO
Then count it again.
